# at412c: maintainer merit request

Use the final source and SHA-256 table in MEASURE-REQUEST-at412.md, section 12.
This lane runs correctness and bounded instruction traces only. All performance
cells below are NOT RUN here. Run on the maintainer's scheduled quiet box.

1. Run all 14 frozen recipes in docs/at412c/merit/generic14.txt through the gate's
   ABBA instrument: PRE versus POST, then POST-layout versus PAD-A. These are the
   standing execfair/bugs5 recipes, including MGET, large values, depth 128, and
   the two mixed cells. Preserve each recipe's score, 4/8-core pin, depth,
   connections and read-local posture. Record rate/latency at matched offered
   load, cycles/op, instructions/op and IPC. The verdict is the instrument's
   per-cell comparison against its measured spread; instruction counts alone
   are not the verdict.
2. Run /home/user/Projects/calib/exec-merit.py's eight cells:
   x2s_a0_unc, x2s_a0_hot, x2s_a1_unc, x2s_a1_hot,
   x1s_a0_unc, x1s_a0_hot, x1s_a1_unc, x1s_a1_hot.
   Compare PRE versus POST with 64 connections, pipeline 4, 16 generator
   threads, three ABBA blocks, 20 seconds per arm. The harness uses 8 server
   cores: 2s/6:2/shards 16 or 1s/read-local 1/shards 64; balancing and auto-FLIP
   off. Uncontended uses private pairs. Hot uses two keys on different owners
   plus four plain INCR clients. Decide by completed EXEC/s at matched load;
   retain plain-writer progress/share, latency, cycles, instructions and IPC.
   Label cost denominators per completed EXEC and per logical INCR separately.
3. Run the T6 contended-script shape for 30 seconds per arm, three ABBA blocks,
   PRE versus POST: 2s, ratio 6:2, shards 16, atomic 0, balancing/auto-FLIP off;
   eight pipeline-1 EVAL clients, four ordinary MULTI/EXEC clients, four
   WATCH/MULTI/EXEC clients, and four plain INCR clients. Every script and EXEC
   increments the same two keys on different owners; plain clients alternate
   those keys. Use the exact WRITE body and client mix in tests/at412.py:storm.
   Separate successful scripts, refused scripts, committed EXECs, aborted WATCH
   attempts and plain writes. Count only successful replies as completed work.
   Decide by successful script/s together with EXEC/writer progress; report
   refusals per arm and exact final-data accounting. Do not hide a change in
   writer share inside an aggregate ops/s or cycles/op denominator.
4. Optional: uncontended two-owner EVAL, p1 and p32, both modes and atomic 0/1,
   PRE versus POST. This prices admission and Final cleanup without contention.

Every arm explicitly sets --databases 1. Keep all other settings and offered
load matched. Require POST script_crossshard_window_refusals=0 and
atomic_txn_order_violations=0; record escalations, escalated commits and FIFO
waits. A crash, missing reply or failed data check invalidates that cell.

PAD-A is type A, a behaviour twin: PRE behaviour in POST-layout's exact common
image. POST-layout and PAD-A have identical section layout and symbol addresses;
only the main-entry jump differs. This controls the common image, not the
smaller ordinary POST executable. Keep the two pairwise comparisons separate.

